.policy "python-security-path-traversal" revision 1
.description "Keep request data that can climb out of a directory, an upload's filename included, out of file paths unless it is reduced to a bare name or the resolved path is checked to stay in its base."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. Client request data (lib/security's sources: Django/DRF `request.GET`/`.POST`/
// `.data`/`.FILES`/…, `self.kwargs` and URL kwargs a `path()`/`re_path()` captures as text, Flask `request.args`/
// `.form`/`.files`/…, Starlette `request.query_params`/`.json()`/…, FastAPI and Flask route parameters, FastAPI
// `UploadFile` parameters) that reaches a filesystem path in a way that can leave its base, in the same function or
// through the project's functions across files, reported at the call that uses the path. An upload's client filename
// is client data: `request.FILES["f"].name`, Flask `request.files["f"].filename`, `UploadFile.filename`.
//
// What the text can do decides, not where it came from. Each value carries one of three shapes:
//   - free text may hold `/`: `../..` or an absolute path escapes (a query parameter, a body field, a filename);
//   - a route parameter bound to one segment (FastAPI `{name}`, Flask `<name>`/`<string:name>`, Django
//     `<str:name>`/`<slug:name>`/`<name>`; never `{name:path}`, `<path:name>`, a regex group) holds no `/`: it climbs
//     only as the whole segment `..`, so beside fixed text in its segment (`f"{name}.json"`, `f"v_{name}"`,
//     `name + ".md"`) it cannot climb and is dropped; `unquote()`, `.replace()`, a decoder or any other library call
//     but a join or a normalisation makes it free text again;
//   - free text after fixed text of its own segment (`f"{user}_{date}_{upload.filename}"`, `f"{uuid}.{ext}"` with
//     `ext = filename.rsplit(".", 1)[-1]`): `x/../../y` must pass through a directory named `{user}_{date}_x`, which
//     the kernel refuses unless it exists. It is reported only where that check is skipped: after a lexical
//     normalisation (`normpath`, `abspath`, `realpath`, `.resolve()`, a method call or slice that may drop the prefix)
//     or at a call that creates the missing directories (`os.makedirs`, `.mkdir(parents=True)`) or normalises the path
//     itself (Django `FileSystemStorage`).
// Fixed text counts when its part of the segment holds a character other than `.` (`f"{name}."` still makes `..`);
// another spliced value next to fixed text counts as a server name.
// The sinks, resolved through imports:
//   - `open`, `io.open`, `codecs.open`, `os.open`, `aiofiles.open`; `os.remove`, `unlink`, `rmdir`, `removedirs`,
//     `mkdir`, `makedirs`, `listdir`, `scandir`, `walk`, `shutil.rmtree`, `glob.glob`/`iglob`; `os.rename`, `replace`,
//     `shutil.copy`, `copy2`, `copyfile`, `copytree`, `move` (source and destination); `shutil.make_archive`'s archive
//     name, `root_dir` and `base_dir`;
//   - readers that open a path they are given: `PIL.Image.open`, pandas `read_csv`/`read_json`/`read_excel`/
//     `read_parquet`/… (`read_pickle` is code-injection's), `zipfile.ZipFile`, `tarfile.open`/`TarFile`;
//   - a pathlib path's `.read_text()`, `.read_bytes()`, `.write_text()`, `.write_bytes()`, `.unlink()`, `.rmdir()`,
//     `.mkdir()`, `.touch()`, `.iterdir()`, `.glob()`, `.rglob()` on any client-derived receiver, and `.open()`,
//     `.rename()`, `.replace()` on one known to be a path (`Path(…)`, `a / b`, `.resolve()`, `.parent`, a name
//     assigned one, a parameter annotated `Path`), so an upload's own `.open()` and `str.replace()` stay apart;
//   - Flask/Werkzeug `send_file(path)` and the directory (never the `path`) of `send_from_directory(directory,
//     path)`; Starlette/FastAPI `FileResponse(path)`; Django `FileSystemStorage(location)`;
//   - Werkzeug `FileStorage.save(dst)` on an upload from `request.files`, Flask-Uploads' `UploadSet.save(upload,
//     name=…, folder=…)`.
// A file-like argument is content, not a path, and never a sink value: an upload object (`request.FILES["f"]`, an
// `UploadFile`/`FileStorage` parameter, `.file`, `.stream`), `io.BytesIO(…)`/`StringIO(…)`.
// Existence oracles (`os.path.exists`/`isfile`/`isdir`/`getsize`/`getmtime`, `os.stat`/`access`, a path's
// `.exists()`/`.is_file()`/`.is_dir()`/`.stat()`) leak only whether a file is there: a separate, weaker message
// (PathProbe), and only where no full sink in the same function takes the same client data.
//   open(os.path.join(MEDIA, request.GET["name"]))                         reported
//   f = request.files["file"]; f.save(os.path.join(UPLOADS, f.filename))   reported
//   send_from_directory(f"static/{group}", path=filename)                  reported: the client picks the directory
//   FileResponse(os.path.join(BASE, name))  with route "/files/{name}"     reported: `..` climbs one level
//   FileResponse(os.path.join(BASE, f"{name}.json"))  same route           not reported: one segment, fixed suffix
//   open(join(BASE, f"{uuid4().hex}.{upload.filename.rsplit('.', 1)[-1]}"), "wb")   not reported
//   send_from_directory(STATIC, filename)                                  not reported: safe_join contains it
//   open(os.path.join(MEDIA, os.path.basename(request.GET["name"])))       not reported
//   Image.open(io.BytesIO(request.FILES["f"].read()))                      not reported: content, not a path
// Sanitisers it trusts: every library call lib/security stops at (`os.path.basename`, `secure_filename`,
// `get_valid_filename`, `safe_join`, a storage's `get_valid_name`/`generate_filename`, `int()`, `uuid4()`,
// `os.path.splitext`…); `Path(x).name`/`.stem`/`.suffix`; a name reassigned from one of those (`name =
// secure_filename(name)`); an upload's `.temporary_file_path()` and `.file` (a server temp file); a pydantic model
// field the model validates (`@field_validator("locale")`, `@validator`, `Field(pattern=…)`) read off a parameter
// annotated with the model; a check call of lib/security (`is_safe_path(p)`, `validate_name(n)`: a checking verb, not
// a function that itself opens the path); and a name its function checks: lib/security's sec_checked (a check call,
// an allow-list `x in …`), a character-class test (`x.isalnum()`, `x.isdigit()`, …), or a containment test on a
// resolved path that reads the name: `.is_relative_to(base)` / `.relative_to(base)` / `os.path.commonpath([...])` /
// `.startswith(base + os.sep)` (or a base ending in `/`) where the tested path comes from `.resolve()`,
// `os.path.realpath`, `abspath` or `normpath`; `x.parent.samefile(base)` / `os.path.samefile`; or a call passing it
// to a function of the run that tests its parameter so (freqtrade's `is_file_in_dir(fn, base)`). For a one-segment
// route parameter, whose only climb is `..`, `startswith(base)` without a separator on its resolved path and a
// `".." in name` / `name == ".."` test also suffice (we-mp-rss `download_cropped_image`). Not sanitisers (they still
// report): `normpath` alone, `.replace("../", "")`, `os.path.commonprefix`, `startswith(base)` without a separator
// on free text, `if ".." in name: raise` on free text (an absolute path passes), and `is_relative_to` on a path never
// resolved.
// Left alone: `send_from_directory(CONST, user_path)`; `default_storage.save(name, f)` and `FileField` uploads
// (Django storages refuse `..`); server-generated names; paths read back from the database; `int()`-cast ids and
// `<int:…>` / `int` route parameters; test files.
// Overlap: none in Ruff or Bandit; Semgrep's Django/Flask path-traversal rules are search-mode `request.$W.get(...)`
// patterns in one function. This rule follows FastAPI parameters, URL kwargs, upload filenames and the project's
// helpers, and reads what part of the path the client text decides.
// Gaps: lib/security's (captures of an `include()`d URLconf's prefix; values stored on objects or in the database;
// calls the call graph cannot resolve; `os.path.dirname()` ends the taint, so `os.makedirs(dirname(p))` before
// `open(p)` is not read for a prefixed upload name). A check is flow-insensitive: a name checked or reassigned to a
// sanitised value anywhere in its function is trusted everywhere in it. A check in a caller does not clear a
// helper's parameter. The text after a value is read for f-strings and `+` only (lib/security's sec_text_after), so a
// one-segment parameter in `"{}.json".format(name)` or `"%s.json" % name` is still reported. A segment's fixed text
// is judged by its characters, so a server value that may be empty or `.` (`f"{prefix}{name}"`) is trusted as a
// name. A route parameter of a router mounted under a prefix that captures it is read as a query parameter (free
// text). Symlinks under the base are not considered. An API meant to expose the whole filesystem (an agent sandbox)
// cannot be told apart.

#include "lib/security.rerail"

// Per file and across files (lib/security's origins): each file states what its file paths take by origin, with the
// value's shape (ptr_val), and a finding reads the cross-file answer by its sink's term (ptr_xfirst): its first
// source. An upload's `.save()` is a sink when the receiver is a Werkzeug upload by another file's say
// (ptr_xupload); a pydantic field another file's model validates, and a helper of the run that tests its parameter
// stays in a base, clear the value by that file's say (gates `ptf:`, and check tokens `pf:`, `pc:`).
.violation PathTraversal(at: node, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "Client data from `{what}` ({p}:{l}) reaches this file path; `..` or an absolute path escapes the base. Keep its basename, or resolve it and check it stays in the base, unless a check elsewhere does."
PathTraversal(c, what, p, l) :- (ptr_sink(c, _) ; ptr_sink_u(c, _, _)), pt_tm(c, ct), ptr_xfirst(ct, k),
    sec_src_info(k, what, p, l).
.violation PathProbe(at: node, what: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) "Client data from `{what}` ({p}:{l}) picks the path this tests, so `..` probes files outside the base. Keep its basename, or resolve it and check it stays in the base, unless a check elsewhere does."
PathProbe(c, what, p, l) :- ptr_probe(c, _), pt_tm(c, ct), ptr_xpfirst(ct, k), sec_src_info(k, what, p, l).
sec_flavor("ptfree"). sec_flavor("ptseg"). sec_flavor("ptlatent").
// ptr_shape_fl(m, fl): the flavor that carries shape m across calls.
.decl ptr_shape_fl(m: symbol, fl: symbol)
ptr_shape_fl("free", "ptfree"). ptr_shape_fl("seg", "ptseg"). ptr_shape_fl("latent", "ptlatent").

// ---- paths -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl ptr_path_q(q: symbol)
ptr_path_q("pathlib.Path"). ptr_path_q("pathlib.PurePath"). ptr_path_q("pathlib.PosixPath").
ptr_path_q("pathlib.PurePosixPath"). ptr_path_q("pathlib.WindowsPath"). ptr_path_q("anyio.Path").
// ptr_path_method(m): pathlib methods that answer another path.
.decl ptr_path_method(m: symbol)
ptr_path_method("resolve"). ptr_path_method("absolute"). ptr_path_method("joinpath"). ptr_path_method("with_name").
ptr_path_method("with_suffix"). ptr_path_method("with_stem"). ptr_path_method("expanduser").
ptr_path_method("relative_to").
// ptr_pathy(e): e's value is a pathlib path.
.decl ptr_pathy(e: node)
ptr_pathy(c) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_path_q(q).
ptr_pathy(b) :- kind(b, "binary_operator"), op(b, "/").
ptr_pathy(p) :- kind(p, "parenthesized_expression"), unparen(p, a), p != a, ptr_pathy(a).
ptr_pathy(w) :- kind(w, "await"), child(w, a, 0), ptr_pathy(a).
ptr_pathy(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, m), ptr_path_method(m), ptr_pathy(o).
ptr_pathy(e) :- attr_of(e, o, "parent"), ptr_pathy(o).
ptr_pathy(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v, _), ptr_pathy(v).
ptr_pathy(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, g), sig_param(g, _, nm, _, _, a, _), text(nm, x),
    text(a, t), match("(Optional\\[)?(pathlib\\.|anyio\\.)?(Pure)?Path\\b.*", t).

// ---- sanitisers and checks ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ptr_clean_q(q): library calls that reduce a value to a bare, safe name or a contained path.
.decl ptr_clean_q(q: symbol)
ptr_clean_q("os.path.basename"). ptr_clean_q("posixpath.basename"). ptr_clean_q("ntpath.basename").
ptr_clean_q("werkzeug.utils.secure_filename"). ptr_clean_q("werkzeug.secure_filename").
ptr_clean_q("django.utils.text.get_valid_filename"). ptr_clean_q("django.utils.text.slugify").
ptr_clean_q("werkzeug.security.safe_join"). ptr_clean_q("werkzeug.utils.safe_join"). ptr_clean_q("flask.safe_join").
ptr_clean_q("flask.helpers.safe_join"). ptr_clean_q("builtins.int"). ptr_clean_q("uuid.UUID").
.decl ptr_clean_method(m: symbol)
ptr_clean_method("get_valid_name"). ptr_clean_method("generate_filename"). ptr_clean_method("get_available_name").
ptr_clean_method("temporary_file_path").
// ptr_name_attr(m): a pathlib path's attributes that hold its last component only.
.decl ptr_name_attr(m: symbol)
ptr_name_attr("name"). ptr_name_attr("stem"). ptr_name_attr("suffix"). ptr_name_attr("suffixes").
// ptr_cut(e): e holds no client path even when what it is built from does. A field of a pydantic model of the run
// that the model validates is cut where the model's file says so (ptr_model_checked0): its read passes a gate
// (ptr_fgate), and a name assigned it a check token (`pf:`).
.decl ptr_cut(e: node)
ptr_cut(e) :- attr_of(e, o, m), ptr_name_attr(m), ptr_pathy(o).
ptr_cut(e) :- attr_of(e, _, "file").
ptr_cut(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, m), ptr_clean_method(m).
// ptr_model_checked0(q, fld): pydantic model q of this file validates field fld (`@field_validator("locale")`,
// `@validator(…)`, `Field(pattern=…)`): mealie's `registration.locale`, read off a parameter annotated with q.
.decl ptr_model_checked0(q: symbol, fld: symbol)
ptr_model_checked0(q, fld) :- class_def(c, q), sec_model_class(c), kind(g, "function_definition"), nearest(g, c, scope),
    dexpr(g, e), unparen(e, dc), kind(dc, "call"), call_name(dc, n), (n = "field_validator" ; n = "validator"),
    posarg(dc, _, s), str(s, fld).
ptr_model_checked0(q, fld) :- class_def(c, q), sec_model_class(c), asg(c, fld, v, _), unparen(v, fc), kind(fc, "call"),
    call_name(fc, "Field"), (sec_arg(fc, -1, "pattern", _) ; sec_arg(fc, -1, "regex", _)).
// ptr_clean(v): v is a sanitised value (ptr_cut, a sanitising library call, or a check call of lib/security).
// ptr_clean_c(v, t): by what another file says (token t): a check call of the run, a pydantic field.
.decl ptr_clean(v: node)
ptr_clean(v) :- unparen(v, e), ptr_cut(e).
ptr_clean(v) :- unparen(v, c), sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_clean_q(q).
ptr_clean(v) :- unparen(v, c), sec_check_call(c).
.decl ptr_clean_c(v: node, t: symbol)
ptr_clean_c(v, t) :- unparen(v, c), sec_check_cond(c, t).
ptr_clean_c(v, cat("pf:", cat(q, cat(":", fld)))) :- unparen(v, e), sec_typed_at(e, q, fld).

// ptr_resolved(e): e is a canonical path: `.resolve()`, os.path.realpath/abspath/normpath, `str()`/`Path()` of one,
// or a name assigned one.
.decl ptr_resolved(e: node)
ptr_resolved(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "resolve").
ptr_resolved(c) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_norm_q(q).
ptr_resolved(c) :- sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "builtins.str" ; q = "os.fspath" ; ptr_path_q(q)), sec_arg(c, 0, _, a),
    ptr_resolved(a).
ptr_resolved(p) :- kind(p, "parenthesized_expression"), unparen(p, a), p != a, ptr_resolved(a).
ptr_resolved(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v, _), ptr_resolved(v).
// ptr_norm_q(q): the lexical normalisations: they fold `x/..` without asking whether x exists.
.decl ptr_norm_q(q: symbol)
ptr_norm_q("os.path.realpath"). ptr_norm_q("os.path.abspath"). ptr_norm_q("os.path.normpath").
ptr_norm_q("posixpath.realpath"). ptr_norm_q("posixpath.abspath"). ptr_norm_q("posixpath.normpath").
// ptr_sep_arg(a): the prefix a `startswith` tests ends in a path separator (`base + os.sep`, `f"{base}/"`,
// `str(base) + "/"`, a name assigned one).
.decl ptr_sw_arg(a: node)
ptr_sw_arg(a) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "startswith"), sec_arg(c, 0, _, a).
ptr_sw_arg(v) :- ptr_sw_arg(r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v, _).
.decl ptr_sep_arg(a: node)
ptr_sep_arg(a) :- ptr_sw_arg(a), text(a, t), contains("sep", t).
ptr_sep_arg(a) :- ptr_sw_arg(a), text(a, t), match("(?s).*/[\"']\\)*", t).
ptr_sep_arg(r) :- ptr_sw_arg(r), kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v, _), ptr_sep_arg(v).
// ptr_contain(h, a): scope h tests that the resolved path a stays under a base.
.decl ptr_contain(h: node, a: node)
ptr_contain(h, o) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, m),
    (m = "is_relative_to" ; m = "relative_to"), ptr_resolved(o), nearest(c, h, fscope).
ptr_contain(h, o) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, "startswith"), ptr_resolved(o),
    sec_arg(c, 0, _, a), ptr_sep_arg(a), nearest(c, h, fscope).
ptr_contain(h, it) :- sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "os.path.commonpath" ; q = "posixpath.commonpath"), sec_arg(c, 0, _, l),
    (kind(l, "list") ; kind(l, "tuple")), child(l, it, _), ptr_resolved(it), nearest(c, h, fscope).
// `x.parent.samefile(base)`, `os.path.samefile(os.path.dirname(x), base)`: the file system compares the real paths.
ptr_contain(h, o) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, "samefile"), nearest(c, h, fscope).
ptr_contain(h, a) :- sec_call_q(c, "os.path.samefile"), sec_arg(c, _, _, a), nearest(c, h, fscope).
// ptr_contain_c(h, a, t): a function of the run that tests its parameter so (`is_path_in_dir(path, base)`) checks
// the argument a that a call in scope h passes it: token `pc:<call's term>:<how>:<index>:<keyword>`, which the
// callee's file decides (ptr_xcparam).
.decl ptr_contain_c(h: node, a: node, t: symbol)
ptr_contain_c(h, a, cat("pc:", cat(ct, cat(":", cat(how, cat(":", cat(to_string(i), ":"))))))) :- call_target(c, _),
    posarg(c, i, a), sec_call_how(c, how), pt_tm(c, ct), nearest(c, h, fscope).
ptr_contain_c(h, a, cat("pc:", cat(ct, cat(":", cat(how, cat(":-1:", k)))))) :- call_target(c, _),
    call_arg(c, -1, k, a), sec_call_how(c, how), pt_tm(c, ct), nearest(c, h, fscope).
// ptr_cparam_sure(g, x), ptr_cparam_tok(g, x, t): def g tests its parameter x stays in a base, surely, or by token t.
.decl ptr_cparam_sure(g: symbol, x: symbol)
ptr_cparam_sure(gq, x) :- pt_def(g, gq), param(g, x, _), ptr_contain(g, a), ptr_reads(a, x).
.decl ptr_cparam_tok(g: symbol, x: symbol, t: symbol)
ptr_cparam_tok(gq, x, t) :- pt_def(g, gq), param(g, x, _), ptr_contain_c(g, a, t), ptr_reads(a, x).
// ptr_xcparam(g, x): the def whose symbol is g tests its parameter x so, across files (a helper calls another).
.decl ptr_xcparam(g: symbol, x: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xcparam(gq, x) :- ptr_cparam_sure(gq, x).
ptr_xcparam(gq, x) :- ptr_cparam_tok(gq, x, t), sec_xchk(t).
// The tokens of this rule: `pc:` the callee tests the parameter the argument lands on (lib/security's mapping);
// `pf:<q>:<f>` model q validates field f.
.decl ptr_tok(t: symbol)
ptr_tok(t) :- ptr_checked_c(_, _, t).
ptr_tok(t) :- ptr_cparam_tok(_, _, t).
sec_xchk(t) :- ptr_tok(t), match("pf:(?<q>[^:]*):(?<fld>.*)", t), ptr_model_checked0(q, fld).
sec_xchk(t) :- ptr_tok(t), match("pc:(?<ct>[^:]*):(?<how>[^:]*):(?<is>[^:]*):(?<k>.*)", t), sec_site(ct, gq),
    i = to_number(is), i >= 0, sec_def_pos(gq, how, i, x), ptr_xcparam(gq, x).
sec_xchk(t) :- ptr_tok(t), match("pc:(?<ct>[^:]*):[^:]*:-1:(?<x>.*)", t), sec_site(ct, gq), sec_def_param(gq, x, _),
    ptr_xcparam(gq, x).
// ptr_reads(a, x): expression a reads name x.
.decl ptr_reads(a: node, x: symbol)
ptr_reads(a, x) :- unparen(a, i), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x).
ptr_reads(a, x) :- within(i, a), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x), !field(_, "attribute", i).
// ptr_checked(h, x): scope h checks or sanitises name x. ptr_checked_c(h, x, t): by token t, which another file
// decides; a name read so passes a gate (sec_ngate "ptr"), a value site a gate (sec_egate "ptr").
.decl ptr_checked(h: node, x: symbol)
ptr_checked(h, x) :- sec_checked(h, x).
ptr_checked(h, x) :- ptr_contain(h, a), ptr_reads(a, x), x != "self", x != "cls", x != "request".
ptr_checked(h, x) :- asg(h, x, v, _), ptr_clean(v), ptr_reads(v, x).
// `x.isalnum()`, `x.isdigit()`, …: a name of letters or digits only holds no separator or dot.
ptr_checked(h, x) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, m), ptr_charclass_method(m),
    unparen(o, i), kind(i, "identifier"), text(i, x), nearest(c, h, fscope).
.decl ptr_checked_c(h: node, x: symbol, t: symbol)
ptr_checked_c(h, x, t) :- sec_checked_c(h, x, t).
ptr_checked_c(h, x, t) :- ptr_contain_c(h, a, t), ptr_reads(a, x), x != "self", x != "cls", x != "request".
ptr_checked_c(h, x, t) :- asg(h, x, v, _), ptr_clean_c(v, t), ptr_reads(v, x).
sec_nchk_c("ptr", h, x, t) :- ptr_checked_c(h, x, t).
sec_echk_c("ptr", e, t) :- sec_value_site(e), ptr_reads(e, x), nearest(e, h, fscope), ptr_checked_c(h, x, t).
.decl ptr_charclass_method(m: symbol)
ptr_charclass_method("isalnum"). ptr_charclass_method("isalpha"). ptr_charclass_method("isdigit").
ptr_charclass_method("isdecimal"). ptr_charclass_method("isnumeric"). ptr_charclass_method("isidentifier").
.decl ptr_checked_expr(e: node)
ptr_checked_expr(e) :- sec_value_site(e), ptr_reads(e, x), nearest(e, h, fscope), ptr_checked(h, x).
// ptr_seg_guard(h, a): scope h stops the one climb a one-segment value has, `..`: `startswith(base)` on its resolved
// path (a separator is not needed, as the value cannot reach a sibling `base-x`), or a `..` test on it.
.decl ptr_seg_guard(h: node, a: node)
ptr_seg_guard(h, o) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, "startswith"), ptr_resolved(o),
    nearest(c, h, fscope).
ptr_seg_guard(h, r) :- cmp_pair(c, _, o, l, r), (o = "in" ; o = "not in"), unparen(l, l2), str(l2, ".."),
    nearest(c, h, fscope).
ptr_seg_guard(h, l) :- cmp_pair(c, _, o, l, r), (o = "==" ; o = "!=" ; o = "in" ; o = "not in"), unparen(r, r2),
    (str(r2, "..") ; has(r2, s, "string"), str(s, "..")), nearest(c, h, fscope).
.decl ptr_guarded(h: node, x: symbol, m: symbol)
ptr_guarded(h, x, "seg") :- ptr_seg_guard(h, a), ptr_reads(a, x).

// ---- what the client text can do in a path ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// The shape of a value (header): "free" may hold `/`; "seg" is one segment, without `/`; "latent" is free text after
// fixed text of its segment.
// ptr_seg_param(f, x): FastAPI or Flask route f binds parameter x to one path segment in every route that names it
// (a Django view's capture: lib/security's sec_xdj_param, of shape "seg" or "free").
.decl ptr_seg_param(f: node, x: symbol)
ptr_seg_param(f, x) :- sec_route_param(f, x, _), ptr_seg_capture(f, x), !ptr_wide_capture(f, x).
.decl ptr_seg_capture(f: node, x: symbol)
ptr_seg_capture(f, x) :- sec_route_param(f, x, _), sec_route(f, "fastapi"), sec_route_decorator(f, _, path),
    contains(cat("{", cat(x, "}")), path).
ptr_seg_capture(f, x) :- sec_route_param(f, x, _), sec_route(f, "flask"), sec_route_decorator(f, _, path),
    (contains(cat("<", cat(x, ">")), path) ; contains(cat("<string:", cat(x, ">")), path) ;
    match(cat("(?s).*<string\\([^>]*\\):", cat(x, ">.*")), path)).
// ptr_wide_capture(f, x): some route of f lets x hold `/`, or captures it with a converter this rule does not know.
.decl ptr_wide_capture(f: node, x: symbol)
ptr_wide_capture(f, x) :- sec_route_param(f, x, _), sec_route(f, "fastapi"), sec_route_decorator(f, _, path),
    contains(cat("{", cat(x, ":")), path).
ptr_wide_capture(f, x) :- sec_route_param(f, x, _), sec_route(f, "flask"), sec_route_decorator(f, _, path),
    contains(cat(":", cat(x, ">")), path), !contains(cat("<string:", cat(x, ">")), path),
    !match(cat("(?s).*<(string|any)\\([^>]*\\):", cat(x, ">.*")), path).

// ptr_prefixed(a) / ptr_suffixed(a): spliced value a has fixed text before / after it in its own path segment, text
// that holds a character other than `.` (or a server value beside literal text), so a cannot be the whole segment.
.decl ptr_prefixed(a: node)
ptr_prefixed(a) :- sec_text_before(_, a, pre), g = @rx_replace(pre, "(?s)^.*[/\\\\]", ""),
    r = @rx_replace(g, "\\{\\}", ""), (match("(?s).*[^.].*", r) ; (contains("{}", g), r != "")).
.decl ptr_suffixed(a: node)
ptr_suffixed(a) :- sec_text_after(_, a, post), g = @rx_replace(post, "(?s)[/\\\\].*$", ""),
    r = @rx_replace(g, "\\{\\}", ""), (match("(?s).*[^.].*", r) ; (contains("{}", g), r != "")).
// ptr_keeps_latent(e): the step into e keeps a fixed prefix in front of the value: building, joining, grouping.
.decl ptr_keeps_latent(e: node)
ptr_keeps_latent(e) :- kind(e, k), (k = "parenthesized_expression" ; k = "await" ; k = "string" ;
    k = "concatenated_string" ; k = "binary_operator" ; k = "conditional_expression" ; k = "boolean_operator" ;
    k = "tuple" ; k = "list" ; k = "set" ; k = "expression_list" ; k = "dictionary" ; k = "list_comprehension" ;
    k = "generator_expression" ; k = "set_comprehension").
ptr_keeps_latent(c) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_join_q(q).
ptr_keeps_latent(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, m), (m = "format" ; m = "join").
.decl ptr_join_q(q: symbol)
ptr_join_q("builtins.str"). ptr_join_q("os.fspath"). ptr_join_q("os.path.join"). ptr_join_q("posixpath.join").
ptr_join_q("builtins.format"). ptr_join_q(q) :- ptr_path_q(q).
// ptr_keeps_seg(e): the step into e adds no `/` to a one-segment value: the above, a slice or index, a string method
// other than `.replace()`/`.translate()`, a normalisation.
.decl ptr_keeps_seg(e: node)
ptr_keeps_seg(e) :- ptr_keeps_latent(e).
ptr_keeps_seg(e) :- kind(e, "subscript").
ptr_keeps_seg(e) :- attr_of(e, _, m), m != "replace", m != "translate".
ptr_keeps_seg(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, m), m != "replace", m != "translate".
ptr_keeps_seg(c) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_norm_q(q).
// ptr_trans(e, a, m, m2): lib/security's step from a to e (sec_step) turns a value of shape m into one of shape m2.
.decl ptr_trans(e: node, a: node, m: symbol, m2: symbol)
ptr_trans(e, a, "free", "free") :- sec_step(e, a), !ptr_cut(e), !ptr_prefixed(a).
ptr_trans(e, a, "free", "latent") :- sec_step(e, a), !ptr_cut(e), ptr_prefixed(a).
ptr_trans(e, a, "latent", "latent") :- sec_step(e, a), !ptr_cut(e), ptr_keeps_latent(e).
ptr_trans(e, a, "latent", "free") :- sec_step(e, a), !ptr_cut(e), !ptr_keeps_latent(e).
ptr_trans(e, a, "seg", "seg") :- sec_step(e, a), !ptr_cut(e), ptr_keeps_seg(e), !ptr_prefixed(a), !ptr_suffixed(a).
ptr_trans(e, a, "seg", "free") :- sec_step(e, a), !ptr_cut(e), !ptr_keeps_seg(e).
// ptr_fgate(e, m, g): e reads a field of a pydantic model of the run (sec_typed_at): a value of shape m passes gate
// g, which holds where the model's file neither types nor validates the field (`G|ptf:<q>:<f>|<m>@<e's term>`).
.decl ptr_fgate(e: node, m: symbol, g: symbol)
ptr_fgate(e, m, cat("G|ptf:", cat(q, cat(":", cat(fld, cat("|", cat(m, cat("@", et)))))))) :- sec_typed_at(e, q, fld),
    pt_tm(e, et), ptr_shape_fl(m, _).
sec_xcond(c) :- sec_xcondq(c), match("ptf:(?<q>[^:]*):(?<fld>.*)", c), !sec_xmodel_typed(q, fld),
    !ptr_model_checked0(q, fld).

// ptr_val(e, o, m): e's value holds client text from origin o, of shape m: lib/security's propagation (sec_step)
// with the sanitisers above cut; a parameter's is what the callers pass in that shape (`P|pt<m>|…`), a call's what
// its function returns (`R|pt<m>|…`).
.decl ptr_val(e: node, o: symbol, m: symbol)
ptr_val(e, o, "free") :- sec_start(e, o).
ptr_val(e, o, m2) :- ptr_trans(e, a, m, m2), !sec_typed_at(e, _, _), ptr_val(a, o, m).
ptr_val(e, g, m2) :- ptr_trans(e, a, m, m2), ptr_fgate(e, m2, g), ptr_val(a, _, m).
sec_gin(g, o) :- ptr_trans(e, a, m, m2), ptr_fgate(e, m2, g), ptr_val(a, o, m).
ptr_val(r, o, m) :- ptr_vin(r, h, x, o, m), !ptr_checked(h, x), !ptr_guarded(h, x, m), !sec_nchk_any("ptr", h, x).
ptr_val(r, g, m) :- ptr_vin(r, h, x, _, m), !ptr_checked(h, x), !ptr_guarded(h, x, m), ptr_shape_fl(m, fl),
    sec_ngate("ptr", fl, h, x, g).
sec_gin(g, o) :- ptr_vin(_, h, x, o, m), !ptr_checked(h, x), !ptr_guarded(h, x, m), ptr_shape_fl(m, fl),
    sec_ngate("ptr", fl, h, x, g).
ptr_val(e, o, m) :- attr_of(e, b, a), sec_validated_attr(a), kind(b, "identifier"), text(b, x), look(b, x, h),
    sec_holder_call(h, x, c), call_arg(c, _, _, v), ptr_val(v, o, m).
ptr_val(c, o, m) :- ptr_shape_fl(m, fl), sec_rorig(c, fl, o).
// ptr_vin(r, h, x, o, m): name r, x as scope h binds it, reads o of shape m before its checks: a value bound to it,
// a parameter's (each shape its callers pass), a FastAPI or Flask route's capture.
.decl ptr_vin(r: node, h: node, x: symbol, o: symbol, m: symbol)
ptr_vin(r, h, x, o, m) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), sec_bind(h, x, v), ptr_val(v, o, m), r != v.
ptr_vin(r, g, x, o, m) :- ptr_shape_fl(m, fl), sec_porig(r, fl, g, x, o).
ptr_vin(r, g, x, k, "seg") :- sec_param_ref(r, g, x), sec_route_param(g, x, p), ptr_seg_param(g, x), sec_key(p, k).
ptr_vin(r, g, x, k, "free") :- sec_param_ref(r, g, x), sec_route_param(g, x, p), !ptr_seg_param(g, x), sec_key(p, k).
// Across files, shape by shape: a parameter holds what a call passes it, or a Django URLconf's capture of its shape;
// a call's value is its function's return where the call passed it client data (any shape) or the function read it.
sec_froute("ptseg", "seg"). sec_froute("ptfree", "free").
sec_fpass(fl, c, a, o) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), ptr_val(a, o, m), ptr_shape_fl(m, fl).
sec_fctx(fl, c, o) :- call_arg(c, _, _, a), ptr_val(a, o, _), ptr_shape_fl(_, fl).
sec_fret(fl, g, o) :- ptr_ret(g, v), ptr_val(v, o, m), ptr_shape_fl(m, fl), !sec_echk_any("ptr", v).
sec_fret(fl, g, eg) :- ptr_ret(g, v), ptr_val(v, _, m), ptr_shape_fl(m, fl), sec_egate("ptr", fl, v, eg).
sec_gin(eg, o) :- ptr_ret(g, v), ptr_val(v, o, m), ptr_shape_fl(m, fl), sec_egate("ptr", fl, v, eg).
.decl ptr_ret(g: node, v: node)
ptr_ret(g, v) :- kind(r, "return_statement"), child(r, v, 0), nearest(r, g, fdef), !ptr_checked_expr(v).

// ---- sinks -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ptr_path_arg(q, i, k): call q takes a path as positional argument i or keyword k.
.decl ptr_path_arg(q: symbol, i: number, k: symbol)
ptr_path_arg("builtins.open", 0, "file"). ptr_path_arg("io.open", 0, "file"). ptr_path_arg("codecs.open", 0, "filename").
ptr_path_arg("os.open", 0, "path"). ptr_path_arg("aiofiles.open", 0, "file"). ptr_path_arg("os.remove", 0, "path").
ptr_path_arg("os.unlink", 0, "path"). ptr_path_arg("os.rmdir", 0, "path"). ptr_path_arg("os.removedirs", 0, "name").
ptr_path_arg("os.mkdir", 0, "path"). ptr_path_arg("os.makedirs", 0, "name"). ptr_path_arg("os.listdir", 0, "path").
ptr_path_arg("os.scandir", 0, "path"). ptr_path_arg("os.walk", 0, "top"). ptr_path_arg("shutil.rmtree", 0, "path").
ptr_path_arg("glob.glob", 0, "pathname"). ptr_path_arg("glob.iglob", 0, "pathname").
ptr_path_arg("flask.send_file", 0, "path_or_file"). ptr_path_arg("flask.helpers.send_file", 0, "path_or_file").
ptr_path_arg("werkzeug.utils.send_file", 0, "path_or_file").
ptr_path_arg("flask.send_from_directory", 0, "directory").
ptr_path_arg("flask.helpers.send_from_directory", 0, "directory").
ptr_path_arg("werkzeug.utils.send_from_directory", 0, "directory").
ptr_path_arg("starlette.responses.FileResponse", 0, "path"). ptr_path_arg("fastapi.responses.FileResponse", 0, "path").
ptr_path_arg("django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage", 0, "location").
ptr_path_arg("django.core.files.storage.filesystem.FileSystemStorage", 0, "location").
ptr_path_arg(q, 0, "src") :- ptr_path_q2(q). ptr_path_arg(q, 1, "dst") :- ptr_path_q2(q).
ptr_path_arg("shutil.make_archive", 0, "base_name"). ptr_path_arg("shutil.make_archive", 2, "root_dir").
ptr_path_arg("shutil.make_archive", 3, "base_dir").
// Readers that open the path they are given (a file-like argument is no path: ptr_filelike).
ptr_path_arg("PIL.Image.open", 0, "fp"). ptr_path_arg("zipfile.ZipFile", 0, "file").
ptr_path_arg("tarfile.open", 0, "name"). ptr_path_arg("tarfile.TarFile", 0, "name").
ptr_path_arg(cat("pandas.read_", f), 0, k) :- ptr_pandas_reader(f, k).
.decl ptr_pandas_reader(f: symbol, k: symbol)
ptr_pandas_reader("csv", "filepath_or_buffer"). ptr_pandas_reader("table", "filepath_or_buffer").
ptr_pandas_reader("fwf", "filepath_or_buffer"). ptr_pandas_reader("json", "path_or_buf").
ptr_pandas_reader("excel", "io"). ptr_pandas_reader("parquet", "path"). ptr_pandas_reader("feather", "path").
ptr_pandas_reader("orc", "path"). ptr_pandas_reader("xml", "path_or_buffer"). ptr_pandas_reader("html", "io").
ptr_pandas_reader("sas", "filepath_or_buffer"). ptr_pandas_reader("stata", "filepath_or_buffer").
ptr_pandas_reader("spss", "path"). ptr_pandas_reader("hdf", "path_or_buf").
// ptr_path_q2(q): the path is the source (first) or the destination (second) argument.
.decl ptr_path_q2(q: symbol)
ptr_path_q2("os.rename"). ptr_path_q2("os.replace"). ptr_path_q2("shutil.copy"). ptr_path_q2("shutil.copy2").
ptr_path_q2("shutil.copyfile"). ptr_path_q2("shutil.copytree"). ptr_path_q2("shutil.move").
// ptr_fs_method(m): pathlib methods no other client-derived value has (a string, an upload).
.decl ptr_fs_method(m: symbol)
ptr_fs_method("read_text"). ptr_fs_method("read_bytes"). ptr_fs_method("write_text"). ptr_fs_method("write_bytes").
ptr_fs_method("unlink"). ptr_fs_method("rmdir"). ptr_fs_method("mkdir"). ptr_fs_method("touch").
ptr_fs_method("iterdir"). ptr_fs_method("glob"). ptr_fs_method("rglob").
// ptr_sink(c, e): call c uses e as a filesystem path.
.decl ptr_sink(c: node, e: node)
ptr_sink(c, e) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_path_arg(q, i, k), (sec_arg(c, i, _, e) ; sec_arg(c, -1, k, e)).
ptr_sink(c, e) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, m), ptr_fs_method(m), unparen(o, e).
ptr_sink(c, e) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, m), (m = "open" ; m = "rename" ;
    m = "replace"), ptr_pathy(o), unparen(o, e).
// ptr_sink_u(c, e, u): call c saves upload u to path e when u is a Werkzeug upload (`request.files[…]`): ptr_xupload,
// by the origins of u's client data.
.decl ptr_sink_u(c: node, e: node, u: node)
ptr_sink_u(c, e, u) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, u, "save"), ptr_val(u, _, _),
    (sec_arg(c, 0, _, e) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "dst", e)).
ptr_sink_u(c, e, u) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "save"), sec_arg(c, 0, _, u),
    ptr_val(u, _, _), (sec_arg(c, -1, "name", e) ; sec_arg(c, -1, "folder", e)).
.decl ptr_xupload(c: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xupload(ct) :- ptr_sink_u(c, _, u), ptr_val(u, o, _), sec_xres(o, k), sec_src_info(k, "request.files", _, _),
    pt_tm(c, ct).
sec_xorig(o) :- ptr_sink_u(_, _, u), ptr_val(u, o, _).
// ptr_latent_sink(c): a sink that reaches a path whose prefixed segment does not exist: it creates the directories
// (`os.makedirs`, `.mkdir(parents=True)`) or normalises the path first (Django `FileSystemStorage`).
.decl ptr_latent_sink(c: node)
ptr_latent_sink(c) :- sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "os.makedirs" ; q = "django.core.files.storage.FileSystemStorage" ;
    q = "django.core.files.storage.filesystem.FileSystemStorage").
ptr_latent_sink(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, "mkdir"), sec_arg(c, -1, "parents", v),
    text(v, "True").
// ptr_probe(c, e): call c tells whether path e exists, or its size or times: an existence oracle.
.decl ptr_probe(c: node, e: node)
ptr_probe(c, e) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_probe_q(q), sec_arg(c, 0, _, e).
ptr_probe(c, e) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, m), (m = "exists" ; m = "is_file" ;
    m = "is_dir" ; m = "stat"), ptr_pathy(o), unparen(o, e).
.decl ptr_probe_q(q: symbol)
ptr_probe_q(cat("os.path.", f)) :- (f = "exists" ; f = "lexists" ; f = "isfile" ; f = "isdir" ; f = "islink" ;
    f = "getsize" ; f = "getmtime" ; f = "getatime" ; f = "getctime").
ptr_probe_q("os.stat"). ptr_probe_q("os.lstat"). ptr_probe_q("os.access").
// ptr_filelike(e): e is file content, not a path: an upload object, `.stream`, an in-memory file.
.decl ptr_filelike(e: node)
ptr_filelike(e) :- unparen(e, c), sec_call_q(c, q), (q = "io.BytesIO" ; q = "io.StringIO").
ptr_filelike(e) :- unparen(e, u), ptr_upload_obj(u).
.decl ptr_upload_obj(e: node)
ptr_upload_obj(e) :- kind(e, "subscript"), field(e, "value", o), sec_source(o, w),
    (w = "request.FILES" ; w = "request.files").
ptr_upload_obj(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, o, "get"), sec_source(o, w),
    (w = "request.FILES" ; w = "request.files").
ptr_upload_obj(e) :- attr_of(e, _, "stream").
ptr_upload_obj(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, h), asg(h, x, v, _), unparen(v, u),
    ptr_upload_obj(u).
ptr_upload_obj(r) :- kind(r, "identifier"), text(r, x), look(r, x, g), sig_param(g, _, nm, _, _, a, _), text(nm, x),
    text(a, t), match("(?s)(Optional\\[)?([A-Za-z_.]*\\.)?(UploadFile|UploadedFile|InMemoryUploadedFile|FileStorage)\\b.*", t).
// sec_sink_fn: a function holding one of these sinks is never a check (lib/security).
sec_sink_fn(gq) :- sec_call_q(c, q), ptr_path_arg(q, _, _), nearest(c, g, fdef), pt_def(g, gq).
sec_sink_fn(gq) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, _, m), ptr_fs_method(m), nearest(c, g, fdef),
    pt_def(g, gq).

// ptr_hit(c, o): sink c, outside test code, takes client text from o in a shape that escapes there (a latent one only
// at a latent sink). ptr_hit_u(c, o): the same of an upload's save (sec_fhit "ptu", ptr_xupload).
.decl ptr_hit(c: node, o: symbol)
ptr_hit(c, o) :- ptr_sink(c, e), ptr_hit_at(c, e, o).
.decl ptr_hit_u(c: node, o: symbol)
ptr_hit_u(c, o) :- ptr_sink_u(c, e, _), ptr_hit_at(c, e, o).
.decl ptr_hit_at(c: node, e: node, o: symbol)
ptr_hit_at(c, e, o) :- (ptr_sink(c, e) ; ptr_sink_u(c, e, _)), !ptr_filelike(e), ptr_val(e, o, m), m != "latent",
    ptr_live(c).
ptr_hit_at(c, e, o) :- (ptr_sink(c, e) ; ptr_sink_u(c, e, _)), ptr_latent_sink(c), ptr_val(e, o, "latent"),
    ptr_live(c).
.decl ptr_live(c: node)
ptr_live(c) :- docof(c, d), !sec_test_doc(d), (ptr_sink(c, _) ; ptr_sink_u(c, _, _) ; ptr_probe(c, _)).
sec_fhit("pt", c, o) :- ptr_hit(c, o).
sec_fhit("ptu", c, o) :- ptr_hit_u(c, o).
// An oracle is reported only where no full sink of the same function takes the same client data (ptr_xfn_hit).
sec_fhit("ptp", c, o) :- ptr_probe(c, e), !ptr_filelike(e), ptr_val(e, o, m), m != "latent", ptr_live(c).
// ptr_scope_at(c, h): sink or oracle c, by its term, sits in scope h (its term).
.decl ptr_scope_at(c: symbol, h: symbol)
ptr_scope_at(ct, ht) :- (ptr_sink(c, _) ; ptr_sink_u(c, _, _) ; ptr_probe(c, _)), nearest(c, h, fscope), pt_tm(c, ct),
    pt_tm(h, ht).
// ptr_xhit(c, k): sink c takes source k; ptr_xfirst(c, k): the least such k. ptr_xprobe(c, k), ptr_xpfirst(c, k):
// the same of an oracle whose scope's sinks take no k.
.decl ptr_xhit(c: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xhit(ct, k) :- sec_xhit("pt", ct, k).
ptr_xhit(ct, k) :- sec_xhit("ptu", ct, k), ptr_xupload(ct).
.decl ptr_xfn_hit(h: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xfn_hit(ht, k) :- ptr_xhit(ct, k), ptr_scope_at(ct, ht).
.decl ptr_xfirst(c: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xfirst(ct, k) :- ptr_xhit(ct, k), !ptr_xlater(ct, k).
.decl ptr_xlater(c: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xlater(ct, k) :- ptr_xhit(ct, k), ptr_xhit(ct, k2), k2 < k.
.decl ptr_xprobe(c: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xprobe(ct, k) :- sec_xhit("ptp", ct, k), ptr_scope_at(ct, ht), !ptr_xfn_hit(ht, k).
.decl ptr_xpfirst(c: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xpfirst(ct, k) :- ptr_xprobe(ct, k), !ptr_xplater(ct, k).
.decl ptr_xplater(c: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
ptr_xplater(ct, k) :- ptr_xprobe(ct, k), ptr_xprobe(ct, k2), k2 < k.

// The cases, `cases/python-security-path-traversal/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "api/__init__.py" from "../cases/python-security-path-traversal/api/__init__.py"
    .fixture "api/cache.py" from "../cases/python-security-path-traversal/api/cache.py"
    .fixture "api/extensions.py" from "../cases/python-security-path-traversal/api/extensions.py"
    .fixture "api/paths.py" from "../cases/python-security-path-traversal/api/paths.py"
    .fixture "api/routes.py" from "../cases/python-security-path-traversal/api/routes.py"
